- **Response before work.** The endpoint sends the same 202 immediately, then looks up the user and sends the email in the background. Existing and unknown accounts take the same time, so timing can't be used to enumerate accounts. If you run serverless, where work after the response can be killed, enqueue a job instead (SQS, BullMQ, pg-boss, etc.). A queue also gives you retries when the email provider has a blip.
